// ===========================================================================
// K SPIDER AI -- Firestore Security Rules  v8.11
// Project  : kspideraimain
// Updated  : October 2026
//
// v8.11 change (PHASE A hardening -- nothing else from v8.10 was removed):
//   1. isAdmin() now also requires request.auth.token.email_verified == true
//      (admin signs in with Google only, so the claim is always true for the
//      real admin; an unverified email/password account using the admin's
//      address can no longer become admin).
//   2. /users/{userId}: a non-admin write can no longer change plan or
//      payment fields (planType, premium, planExpiry, paidAmount,
//      paymentStatus) away from their current value, can no longer touch
//      paymentMethod / paymentId / accessStart / disabled / suspended /
//      suspendReason / adminNote, and can no longer write toolAccess_<tool>.
//      A NEW user doc may only be created with default (free / unpaid)
//      values. Writes that leave those fields unchanged (e.g. Google login
//      re-saving the same plan values) still work. Read access and every
//      other field are unchanged on purpose (Phase B will tighten them after
//      the separate tool pages are checked).
//      >>> WHEN A NEW TOOL IS ADDED TO THE SITE, ADD ITS ID TO
//      >>> toolAccessKeys() BELOW, otherwise a user could write
//      >>> toolAccess_<newtool> themselves.
//   3. /otp_store: admin only (the OTP flow was removed -- login is now
//      Google Sign-In only).
//   4. /payments create: only a request-style document is accepted
//      (status 'pending', userEmail + orderId present). A client can no
//      longer create a payment that is already 'approved'.
//   5. userSafeFields() (unused helper) no longer lists plan/payment keys.
//
// v8.10 change: /rto_agent_requests/{refId} -- the RTO Exam Pro tool may now
// record an approved agent's short link code (_shortCode + linkGeneratedAt)
// ONCE, only after admin approval, and only if no code is saved yet. This lets
// old "?k=CODE" promo links resolve from the cloud on any device. Nothing else
// from v8.9 was changed.
//
// v8.9 change: added the K SPIDER DOCTOR AI block (/doctors/{doctorId} plus
// its private subcollections, and /doctorSignupRequests). This gives the
// Doctor AI tool three things it was missing: real per-doctor data isolation
// (no doctor can reach another's patients), cross-device access (patient data
// lives in Firestore under the doctor's UID instead of only in one browser's
// localStorage), and an admin approval gate (a new signup is locked to
// approvalStatus:'pending' and cannot self-approve). Nothing else from v8.8
// was changed.
//
// v8.8 change: bcJobApplications now also lets a job's poster read the
// applications for THAT job (request.auth.uid matched against the job
// doc's postedByAuthUid via get()) -- needed for BrahminConnect's "View
// Applicants" list, which was previously only readable by the applicant
// themselves or admin. Nothing else changed from v8.7.
//
// v8.7 change: added rules for BrahminConnect's collections (bcBiodata,
// bcBusiness, bcJobs, bcJobApplications, bc_reports, bcSuccessStories,
// bcInterests, bcShortlists, bcBlocks). BrahminConnect is a SEPARATE tool
// from Brahmin Vivaah, sharing this same project/login on purpose (so
// members stay logged in across both) but using its own "bc"-prefixed
// collections so its data never mixes with Brahmin Vivaah's. Same
// Anonymous-Auth + ownerAuthUid security model as /brahminBiodata below,
// nothing else in v8.6 was touched.
// ===========================================================================
//
// +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
// |  WHAT CHANGED: v8.4 -> v8.5 -- SECURITY HARDENING for Brahmin Vivaah      |
// +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
// |  v8.4 gave Brahmin Vivaah collections the SAME "isOwner() || true"      |
// |  document-ID-is-identity model already used sitewide. That's an        |
// |  accepted trade-off for most tools here, but for a matrimony tool it    |
// |  means anyone who can compute someone's sanitised-email doc ID (that    |
// |  ID isn't random -- it IS their email, lightly escaped) could read       |
// |  their phone number and address directly, bypassing the "reveal after  |
// |  accepted interest" flow in the app entirely.                          |
// |                                                                         |
// |  v8.5 fixes this WITHOUT touching your OTP login or any other tool:     |
// |                                                                         |
// |  - The tool now also signs every visitor in with Firebase Anonymous    |
// |    Auth (silent, free, no backend). This gives Firestore rules a REAL  |
// |    request.auth.uid to check server-side -- something OTP alone         |
// |    can't provide.                                                      |
// |                                                                         |
// |  - /brahminBiodata/{userId} now only holds public-safe biodata fields. |
// |    Writes require request.auth.uid == the doc's own ownerAuthUid       |
// |    (set once, from a real anon-auth session) instead of "anyone who    |
// |    knows the ID."                                                      |
// |                                                                         |
// |  - NEW /brahminBiodata/{userId}/private/contact -- mobile, WhatsApp,    |
// |    email, address, reference. CLOSED by default. Readable only by the  |
// |    verified owner, admin, or an authUid the owner explicitly added to  |
// |    allowedReaderAuthUids (done automatically by the app once both      |
// |    sides of an interest have accepted -- see bvGrantContactAccess in    |
// |    the tool). No amount of doc-ID guessing exposes this collection.    |
// |                                                                         |
// |  - /interests/{pairId} create/update now require the real authUid of   |
// |    the sender (create) or of the sender/recipient-owner (update) --     |
// |    no longer "anyone can flip any interest's status."                  |
// |                                                                         |
// |  - /shortlists/{userId} and /blocks/{userId} ownership now checked      |
// |    against the matching biodata doc's real ownerAuthUid.               |
// |                                                                         |
// |  Trade-off to know about: Anonymous Auth sessions are tied to a        |
// |  browser/device (Firebase persists them in IndexedDB). If someone      |
// |  clears site data or switches devices, they get a new authUid and      |
// |  won't automatically own their old biodata doc anymore -- they'd need   |
// |  the admin to reassign ownerAuthUid for them from the Brahmin Vivaah   |
// |  admin panel (a manual "recover my profile" support step, not          |
// |  something the rules can solve on their own without adding a real      |
// |  backend/Cloud Function -- which would be the fully complete fix but    |
// |  needs a paid Firebase plan and server code).                          |
// |                                                                         |
// |  ALL OTHER RULES -- identical to v8.4, not touched.                     |
// +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
// ===========================================================================

rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // HELPER FUNCTIONS
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------

    // v8.11: email_verified added. The admin signs in with Google, which
    // always sets email_verified = true.
    function isAdmin() {
      return request.auth != null
          && request.auth.token.email == 'kspider221206@gmail.com'
          && request.auth.token.email_verified == true;
    }

    function isLoggedIn() {
      return request.auth != null;
    }

    function emailToKey(email) {
      return email
        .replace('.', '_').replace('.', '_').replace('.', '_')
        .replace('.', '_').replace('.', '_').replace('.', '_')
        .replace('.', '_').replace('.', '_').replace('.', '_')
        .replace('.', '_')
        .replace('#', '_').replace('#', '_')
        .replace('$', '_').replace('$', '_')
        .replace('/', '_').replace('/', '_')
        .replace('[', '_').replace('[', '_')
        .replace(']', '_').replace(']', '_');
    }

    // NOTE (Phase B): the trailing "|| true" is still here on purpose. It is
    // removed in Phase B, together with a corrected emailToKey(), once the
    // separate tool pages have been checked so that nothing that reads
    // /users/{key} without a login breaks.
    function isOwner(docId) {
      return docId != null && docId != ''
        && (
          (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == docId)
          || (request.auth != null && emailToKey(request.auth.token.email) == docId)
          || true
        );
    }

    // v8.11: plan / payment keys removed -- only the admin may write those.
    function userSafeFields() {
      return [
        'name', 'mobile', 'email',
        'country', 'state', 'city', 'cityPin',
        'language', 'photoURL', 'loginMethod',
        'loginCount', 'lastLogin', 'lastSeen',
        'updatedAt', 'registeredAt', 'verifiedAt', 'createdAt',
        'toolsUsed', 'lastToolUsed', 'timeSpentMins',
        'verified', 'source',
        'pendingPlan', 'pendingOrderId',
        'profession', 'bio'
      ];
    }

    // v8.11: fields only the admin may set on a /users document.
    function userLockedKeys() {
      return [
        'paymentMethod', 'paymentId', 'accessStart',
        'disabled', 'suspended', 'suspendReason', 'adminNote'
      ];
    }

    // v8.11: per-tool paid-access keys (toolAccess_<toolId>), written only by
    // the admin when a tool payment is approved. Firestore rules cannot match
    // a key prefix, so every tool id is listed here. ADD A NEW TOOL'S ID HERE
    // WHEN IT LAUNCHES.
    function toolAccessKeys() {
      return [
        'toolAccess_whatsapp-bulk-sender',
        'toolAccess_resume-builder',
        'toolAccess_image-master-pro',
        'toolAccess_ai-teacher',
        'toolAccess_dr-shreyansh-academy',
        'toolAccess_ai-business-consultant',
        'toolAccess_ai-prompt-engine',
        'toolAccess_ai-file-converter',
        'toolAccess_pharmacy-master',
        'toolAccess_pharma-marketing-tool',
        'toolAccess_india-fbook',
        'toolAccess_linkshare',
        'toolAccess_multipost',
        'toolAccess_brahmin-vivaah',
        'toolAccess_brahminconnect',
        'toolAccess_doctor-elite-pro-max',
        'toolAccess_kspider-doctor-ai-v3',
        'toolAccess_kspider-400-tools',
        'toolAccess_knowledge-spider',
        'toolAccess_wa-broadcast-pro',
        'toolAccess_free-ai-video-generator',
        'toolAccess_cybershield-pro',
        'toolAccess_lead-scout',
        'toolAccess_webcraft-pro',
        'toolAccess_script-studio',
        'toolAccess_file-analyzer-pro',
        'toolAccess_review-booster-pro',
        'toolAccess_voxai-pro',
        'toolAccess_rto-exam-pro',
        'toolAccess_kspider-connect-jobs',
        'toolAccess_ks-trademind',
        'toolAccess_kspider-tools-features-adv-prompt',
        'toolAccess_kspider-social-prompt-generator',
        'toolAccess_universal-business-marketing-pro',
        'toolAccess_gujarat-govt-form-assistant'
      ];
    }

    // v8.11: on UPDATE, plan/payment values must come back exactly as they
    // are stored (a missing field counts as its default, so re-saving the
    // default value on an old doc is fine).
    function planFieldsUnchanged() {
      return request.resource.data.get('planType', 'free')      == resource.data.get('planType', 'free')
          && request.resource.data.get('premium', false)         == resource.data.get('premium', false)
          && request.resource.data.get('planExpiry', null)       == resource.data.get('planExpiry', null)
          && request.resource.data.get('paidAmount', 0)          == resource.data.get('paidAmount', 0)
          && request.resource.data.get('paymentStatus', 'none')  == resource.data.get('paymentStatus', 'none');
    }

    // v8.11: on CREATE, a user doc may only start in the free / unpaid state.
    function newUserIsUnprivileged() {
      return request.resource.data.get('planType', 'free')      == 'free'
          && request.resource.data.get('premium', false)         == false
          && request.resource.data.get('planExpiry', null)       == null
          && request.resource.data.get('paidAmount', 0)          == 0
          && request.resource.data.get('paymentStatus', 'none')  == 'none'
          && !request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(userLockedKeys())
          && !request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(toolAccessKeys());
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /users/{userId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin() || isOwner(userId);
      allow create: if isAdmin()
                    || (isOwner(userId) && newUserIsUnprivileged());
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || (
                          isOwner(userId)
                       && planFieldsUnchanged()
                       && !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                            .affectedKeys().hasAny(userLockedKeys())
                       && !request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                            .affectedKeys().hasAny(toolAccessKeys())
                       );
      allow delete: if isAdmin();

      match /toolHistory/{entryId} {
        allow read:   if isAdmin() || isOwner(userId);
        allow create: if isAdmin() || isOwner(userId);
        allow update: if isAdmin();
        allow delete: if isAdmin();
      }

      match /notifications/{notifId} {
        allow read:   if isAdmin() || isOwner(userId);
        allow create: if isAdmin();
        allow update: if isAdmin()
                      || (
                            isOwner(userId)
                         && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                              .affectedKeys()
                              .hasOnly(['read', 'readAt'])
                         );
        allow delete: if isAdmin() || isOwner(userId);
      }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /payments/{paymentId}
    // v8.11: create only as a pending request (never as already approved).
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /payments/{paymentId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin()
                    || (
                          isLoggedIn()
                       && resource.data.userEmail == request.auth.token.email
                       );
      allow create: if isAdmin()
                    || (
                          request.resource.data.status == 'pending'
                       && request.resource.data.userEmail is string
                       && request.resource.data.orderId is string
                       );
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /tools/{toolId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /tools/{toolId} {
      allow read:  if true;
      allow write: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /admin/{docId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /admin/{docId} {
      allow read:  if true;
      allow write: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /ads/{adId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /ads/{adId} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin();
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                         .affectedKeys()
                         .hasOnly(['clicks', 'impressions']);
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /adRequests/{docId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /adRequests/{docId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin();
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                         .affectedKeys()
                         .hasOnly(['status', 'updatedAt']);
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /approved_advertisers/{advKey}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /approved_advertisers/{advKey} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin();
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /instituteRequests/{docId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /instituteRequests/{docId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                         .affectedKeys()
                         .hasOnly([
                           'status',         'updatedAt',
                           'approvedAt',     'rejectedAt',
                           'banStatus',      'banReason',
                           'bannedAt',       'unbannedAt',
                           'permissionDate', 'expireDate'
                         ]);
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /students/{studentId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /students/{studentId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin() || true;
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                         .affectedKeys()
                         .hasOnly([
                           'name', 'phone', 'email', 'city', 'state',
                           'goal', 'lastSeen', 'updatedAt', 'source', 'toolUrl'
                         ]);
      allow delete: if isAdmin();

      match /exams/{examId} {
        allow read:   if isAdmin() || true;
        allow create: if true;
        allow update: if isAdmin();
        allow delete: if isAdmin();
      }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /franchise_inquiries/{docId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /franchise_inquiries/{docId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin();
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /franchise_dedupe/{emailKey}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /franchise_dedupe/{emailKey} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if true;
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /announcements/{docId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /announcements/{docId} {
      allow read:  if true;
      allow write: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /otp_store/{docId}
    // v8.11: OTP login was removed (Google Sign-In only) -- admin access only.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /otp_store/{docId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /admin_notifications/{docId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /admin_notifications/{docId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin();
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /user_api_keys/{safeEmailId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /user_api_keys/{safeEmailId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin() || isOwner(safeEmailId);
      allow create: if isAdmin() || isOwner(safeEmailId);
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || (
                          isOwner(safeEmailId)
                       && request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                            .affectedKeys()
                            .hasOnly([
                              'claude', 'groq', 'gemini',
                              'gai', 'openai',
                              'addedAt', 'updatedAt'
                            ])
                       );
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /wa_referrals/{shortCode}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /wa_referrals/{shortCode} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                         .affectedKeys()
                         .hasOnly(['updatedAt']);
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /wa_ref_notifs/{shortCode}/messages/{msgId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /wa_ref_notifs/{shortCode}/messages/{msgId} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin();
      allow update: if true;
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /rto_agent_requests/{refId}
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /rto_agent_requests/{refId} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                         .affectedKeys()
                         .hasOnly([
                           'updatedAt', 'source',
                           '_seen',     'logo'
                         ])
                    // v8.10: RTO tool may record the agent's short link code ONCE,
                    // only after admin has approved, and only if none is saved yet.
                    || (
                         request.resource.data.diff(resource.data)
                           .affectedKeys()
                           .hasOnly(['_shortCode', 'linkGeneratedAt'])
                         && resource.data.get('status', '') == 'approved'
                         && resource.data.get('_shortCode', '') == ''
                         && request.resource.data.get('_shortCode', '') is string
                         && request.resource.data.get('_shortCode', '').size() <= 12
                       );
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /brahminBiodata/{userId}   --  v8.4 -> v8.5 tightened
    //
    // PUBLIC-SAFE fields only (name, photo, Gotra, Nakshatra, education,
    // city, etc.) live on this top-level doc -- open read is fine, this is
    // exactly what "Browse Matches" is meant to show.
    //
    // Contact-sensitive fields (mobile, WhatsApp, email, address,
    // reference) are NOT stored here anymore -- see /private/contact below.
    //
    // doc ID = emailToKey(account email) -- kept for admin search &
    // one-profile-per-account consistency. But WRITE access is no longer
    // "whoever knows the ID" -- every write must carry a real, Firebase
    // Anonymous-Auth-verified request.auth.uid matching the stored
    // ownerAuthUid. Anonymous Auth is free and needs no backend; the app
    // signs every visitor in silently on load, on top of (not replacing)
    // the existing OTP/K Spider AI session.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /brahminBiodata/{userId} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
      // v8.5 -> v8.6: transitional clause added. Any doc saved before this
      // security round (or before Anonymous Auth was enabled) has no
      // ownerAuthUid field yet, permanently locking that account out with
      // no way to self-heal. If ownerAuthUid is missing, the FIRST update
      // is allowed to claim it (exactly like a fresh create) -- after that
      // one-time claim, only the matching authUid can update again. This
      // does not reopen the old "anyone can write" hole: it only accepts
      // a real, Anonymous-Auth-verified uid, and only until the field is
      // set once.
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid)
                    || (request.auth != null && !('ownerAuthUid' in resource.data));
      allow delete: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid);

      // Contact-sensitive fields. CLOSED by default -- readable only by the
      // verified owner, the admin, or a visitor whose real authUid the
      // owner has explicitly added to allowedReaderAuthUids (done by the
      // app automatically once both sides have an accepted /interests
      // record -- see bbRespondInterest / bvGrantContactAccess in the tool).
      match /private/contact {
        allow read:   if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid)
                      || (request.auth != null && resource.data.allowedReaderAuthUids is list
                          && request.auth.uid in resource.data.allowedReaderAuthUids);
        allow create: if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
        allow update: if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
        allow delete: if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
      }

      // "Who viewed my profile" log
      match /profileViews/{viewerId} {
        allow read:   if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/brahminBiodata/$(userId)).data.ownerAuthUid);
        allow create: if true;
        allow update: if isAdmin();
        allow delete: if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/brahminBiodata/$(userId)).data.ownerAuthUid);
      }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /interests/{pairId}   --  v8.4 -> v8.5 tightened
    //
    // "Express interest" between two Brahmin Vivaah members. pairId is
    // deterministic -- [keyA, keyB].sort().join('_') -- so there's at most
    // one record per pair and no query/index is needed to check status.
    //
    // create: the sender must prove they really are who they claim
    // (fromAuthUid) with a real authUid. update (status change + recording
    // toAuthUid): only the original sender OR the verified owner of the
    // recipient's biodata may update -- i.e. only the two people involved.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /interests/{pairId} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.fromAuthUid);
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.fromAuthUid)
                    || (request.auth != null
                        && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/brahminBiodata/$(resource.data.toUid)).data.ownerAuthUid);
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /shortlists/{userId} and /blocks/{userId}   --  v8.4 -> v8.5 tightened
    //
    // Per-user arrays (uids / blockedUids). Ownership now checked against
    // the matching biodata doc's real ownerAuthUid, same model as above.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /shortlists/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin()
        || (request.auth != null
            && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/brahminBiodata/$(userId))
            && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/brahminBiodata/$(userId)).data.ownerAuthUid);
    }
    match /blocks/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin()
        || (request.auth != null
            && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/brahminBiodata/$(userId))
            && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/brahminBiodata/$(userId)).data.ownerAuthUid);
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /brahmin_reports/{docId}
    //
    // User-submitted profile reports for Brahmin Vivaah. Managed from the
    // Brahmin Vivaah panel in admin.html.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /brahmin_reports/{docId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin();
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /successStories/{docId}
    //
    // Opt-in success-story submissions for Brahmin Vivaah. Public read
    // only once isAdmin() sets approved:true from the admin panel.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /successStories/{docId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin() || resource.data.approved == true;
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // =========================================================================
    // BrahminConnect (v8.7) -- a SEPARATE tool from Brahmin Vivaah above.
    // Same project/login on purpose (members stay logged in across both),
    // but its own "bc"-prefixed collections so data never mixes with
    // Brahmin Vivaah's. Same Anonymous-Auth + ownerAuthUid model as
    // /brahminBiodata above.
    // =========================================================================

    // ---- Vivaah module ----
    match /bcBiodata/{userId} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid)
                    || (request.auth != null && !('ownerAuthUid' in resource.data)); // transitional self-heal, same as brahminBiodata
      allow delete: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid);

      match /private/contact {
        allow read:   if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid)
                      || (request.auth != null && resource.data.allowedReaderAuthUids is list
                          && request.auth.uid in resource.data.allowedReaderAuthUids);
        allow create: if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
        allow update: if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
        allow delete: if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
      }

      match /bcProfileViews/{viewerId} {
        allow read:   if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/bcBiodata/$(userId)).data.ownerAuthUid);
        allow create: if true;
        allow update: if isAdmin();
        allow delete: if isAdmin()
                      || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/bcBiodata/$(userId)).data.ownerAuthUid);
      }
    }

    match /bcInterests/{pairId} {
      allow read:   if true;
      allow create: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == request.resource.data.fromAuthUid);
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.fromAuthUid)
                    || (request.auth != null
                        && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/bcBiodata/$(resource.data.toUid)).data.ownerAuthUid);
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    match /bcShortlists/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin()
        || (request.auth != null
            && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/bcBiodata/$(userId))
            && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/bcBiodata/$(userId)).data.ownerAuthUid);
    }
    match /bcBlocks/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin()
        || (request.auth != null
            && exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/bcBiodata/$(userId))
            && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/bcBiodata/$(userId)).data.ownerAuthUid);
    }

    match /bc_reports/{docId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin();
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    match /bcSuccessStories/{docId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin() || resource.data.approved == true;
      allow create: if true;
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // ---- Business Directory module ----
    match /bcBusiness/{docId} {
      allow read: if resource.data.status == 'approved'
                  || isAdmin()
                  || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid);
      allow create: if request.auth != null;
      allow update, delete: if isAdmin()
                             || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.ownerAuthUid);

      match /bcRatings/{ratingId} {
        allow read: if true;
        allow write: if request.auth != null;
      }
    }

    // ---- Jobs module ----
    match /bcJobs/{docId} {
      allow read: if resource.data.status == 'active'
                  || isAdmin()
                  || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.postedByAuthUid);
      allow create: if request.auth != null;
      allow update, delete: if isAdmin()
                             || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.postedByAuthUid);
    }

    match /bcJobApplications/{docId} {
      allow create: if request.auth != null;
      // v8.8: also let the job's poster read applications for their own job
      // (needed for the "View Applicants" list) -- the query is always
      // filtered by jobId, so Firestore can resolve this get() safely.
      allow read: if isAdmin()
                  || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == resource.data.applicantOwnerAuthUid)
                  || (request.auth != null
                      && request.auth.uid == get(/databases/$(database)/documents/bcJobs/$(resource.data.jobId)).data.postedByAuthUid);
    }

    // =========================================================================
    // K SPIDER DOCTOR AI  (v8.9)  --  clinic management tool for doctors
    //
    // /doctors/{doctorId}  where doctorId == the doctor's Firebase Auth UID.
    //
    // THREE things this block guarantees:
    //
    //  1. DATA ISOLATION. A doctor can only ever read/write their OWN record
    //     and their OWN patient data. There is no rule path that lets one
    //     doctor reach another doctor's documents, so "everyone sees the same
    //     data" becomes impossible at the database level, not just in the UI.
    //
    //  2. CROSS-DEVICE. Because patients/appointments/prescriptions now live
    //     in Firestore subcollections under the doctor's UID (instead of only
    //     in that browser's localStorage), the same login on any device or
    //     location loads the same data.
    //
    //  3. ADMIN APPROVAL. A new signup can only ever create itself as
    //     approvalStatus:'pending' and can never promote itself. Only the
    //     admin can flip it to 'approved' (or 'rejected'/'suspended'), so an
    //     unapproved doctor cannot get in by editing client-side code.
    // =========================================================================
    match /doctors/{doctorId} {

      // Admin sees every doctor (needed for the approval queue + list view).
      // A doctor sees only themselves -- including their own approvalStatus,
      // which is what the tool checks to decide whether to let them in.
      allow read: if isAdmin()
                  || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == doctorId);

      // Self-registration only, and only in a locked-down initial state:
      // always 'pending' approval, always the 'trial' plan, always zero
      // usage. Nothing here can be talked up by editing the client.
      allow create: if request.auth != null
                    && request.auth.uid == doctorId
                    && request.resource.data.approvalStatus == 'pending'
                    && request.resource.data.plan == 'trial'
                    && request.resource.data.status == 'trial'
                    && request.resource.data.rxCount == 0;

      // Admin may change anything (approve / reject / suspend / upgrade).
      // The doctor may edit their own profile fields and their own rxCount,
      // but the four privilege fields must come back BYTE-IDENTICAL, so a
      // doctor can never self-approve or self-upgrade.
      allow update: if isAdmin()
                    || (request.auth != null
                        && request.auth.uid == doctorId
                        && request.resource.data.approvalStatus == resource.data.approvalStatus
                        && request.resource.data.plan    == resource.data.plan
                        && request.resource.data.status  == resource.data.status
                        && request.resource.data.rxLimit == resource.data.rxLimit);

      // Only the admin can remove a doctor account.
      allow delete: if isAdmin();

      // Everything under a doctor -- patients, appointments, prescriptions,
      // invoices, queue, settings -- is private to that doctor (and admin for
      // support). One recursive rule covers every current and future
      // subcollection, so adding a new one later needs no rules change.
      match /{docData=**} {
        allow read, write: if isAdmin()
                           || (request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == doctorId);
      }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /doctorSignupRequests/{doctorId}
    //
    // A small, admin-readable mirror of each new signup, so the admin panel
    // can show a "new doctor is waiting for approval" queue without needing
    // to relax read access on /doctors itself. Written once by the doctor at
    // signup; only the admin can read the queue or clear an entry.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /doctorSignupRequests/{doctorId} {
      allow read:   if isAdmin();
      allow create: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == doctorId;
      allow update: if isAdmin();
      allow delete: if isAdmin();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // /ai_rate_limits/{docId}  -- Cloud Function only, no browser access
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /ai_rate_limits/{docId} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // DEFAULT DENY
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }

  }
}
